     * projections such as Maximum Intensity Projection (MIP), Minimum Intensity Projection (MinIP), Average Intensity Projection (AIP),
     * or Median Intensity Projection (MedIP), depending on the provided option. If the option is an integer, it saves the corresponding
     * slice. If the option is a string, it saves the specified projection. If no option is provided, it defaults to saving all slices
     * along the specified plane. The function checks for valid inputs and handles the creation of the output directory if it does not
     * exist. It utilizes the filesystem (fs) library for directory operations and the stb_image_write library for saving images.
     *
     * @param path: A string representing the output directory where the slices or projections will be saved.
     * @param plane: A string specifying the plane of the slices or projections ('x-y', 'x-z', 'y-z').
