following. Let's say that I split my file in chunks (they are not some entity but for easier understanding) of blocks in a way that:
- Every chunk fits in the intermediate memory segment.
- Sort the records of every chunk
- Rewrite the block of every chunk back to data.db.
This procedure achieves the splitting of the file into chunk in order to:
- sort the records in each block
- sort the records between blocks in a chunk
note: there is no sorting between chunks.
Then B-Way merging comes into place. If I have B+1 memory slots and I want to merge B chunks you do the following:
- Keep 1 block from each chunk in memory
- Load from every chunk of the hard disk the block with the smallest values
- Merge by taking the smallest item of each block that is loaded in memory and add it to the output block in memory
- If output block is full then flash to disk.
- If chunk page is full, load next page of chunk.
